# CHANGELOG

Session journal for SLIME-UI / NNUI_CELL (MIVIM Development — *Standards in
Novel Design*). Entries are numbered `## YYYY-MM-DD: NNN`, oldest first.
Source of record for the full narrative is `logs/devlog`; this file is the
condensed, consumable history.

---

## 2026-07-19: 001 — Genesis: NNLG concept, roles, anti-drift, theory core

Project founded from the cornstarch-and-water insight: replace the box model
with a single continuous medium governed by non-Newtonian (yield-stress fluid)
physics. Established in this session:

- **Naming**: SLIME is the application identity; NNLG (non-Newtonian Liquid
  Glass) is the method name.
- **Roles**: Claude (FABLE5) is master developer (research, technical design,
  rigor); Heat is creative lead and user-feature executive (design authority,
  creative direction).
- **Pipeline standard**: research → paper → theory → planning → development →
  application. No stage-skipping.
- **Anti-drift principle** (load-bearing): novel design must not decay into
  "what works"; sub-agents water down what they don't understand. Enforced by
  artifacts (invariants-as-tests), not intentions.
- **"Settled" defined** (creative lead): the UI has stopped self-adjusting —
  like cornstarch fluid coming to rest in a bowl. Formalized as a measurable
  strain-rate threshold, not a duration.
- **Theory core**: energy functional `E = E_fill + E_cohesion + E_content`
  damped by thixotropic viscosity; content as rigid inclusions in a
  yield-stress matrix; continuum-over-boxes as the central thesis; theming as
  a shader over one medium.
- **Draft invariants 1–5**: no authored positions; real Herschel–Bulkley per
  frame; locks are yield-stress fields not flags; threshold-terminated
  settling; one medium.
- **Research gates defined**: R1 discretization (50 regions < 16 ms/frame),
  R2 determinism (bit-identical settles), R3 agent grammar (< ~80 tokens per
  layout). Explicitly deferred: OS integration, multi-user, CSS interop,
  scale beyond 50 regions.
- Tool primitives sketched: t1 `slime-lock`, t2 `window-lock`, t3 `isolation`.

## 2026-07-19: 002 — The cell reframe: NNUI_CELL and the two-axis model

Major thematic reframing by the creative lead: the project becomes
**NNUI_CELL** (non-Newtonian User Interface Cell). SLIME is reassigned as a
*trait* of the Cell.

- **Two-axis model**: rheological axis (how it flows — HB law, solidity,
  settling) + genetic axis (what it becomes — genome, expression, phenotype).
  Expressive power is the product, not the sum, of the axes.
- **Genetic axis formalized**: `phenotype = express(genome)`; asset
  assimilation = pure sequencing function (bytes in, trait-set out);
  polymorphic rendering via an extensible expression registry; mitosis
  reduced to genome-copy + independent re-expression (child inherits no
  geometry — settles under its own local pressure).
- **Germline decision**: cells are never empty; absence of absorbed data is
  the germline genome Γ₀ expressing primitive phenotypes. One code path;
  default UI is the same substance as user UI.
- **Invariant 7 added**: every biological term must reduce to a defined
  deterministic mechanism before entering the spec.
- **R4 added** (expression registry gate); R3 sharpened to two verb families
  (rheological + genetic).
- **Course correction (user-forced)**: a proposed "ambient gene-sharing on
  proximity" option was correctly rejected as contradicting frozen
  requirements — it reduces to nondeterminism, which R2 and Invariant 7
  forbid. Recorded as normative: the boundary carries two decoupled
  coefficients — material diffusion D (always on) and gene transfer
  (**default off, opt-in only, deliberate bind operation**). Nothing
  stochastic anywhere in the genetic path; adjacency never moves genes.
- **Theory frozen** at the gate. Decision: next artifact is the formal Proof
  of Concept paper, then the R1+R2 prototype.

## 2026-07-19: 003 — NNUI_CELL_PoC v0.1: the formal specification

Wrote and typeset the canonical PoC paper (11 pages, LaTeX → PDF, now at
`latex/v0.1/NNUI_CELL_PoC_v0.1.tex`). Real technical contribution beyond the
brainstorm:

- **Dual-rate yield resolution** (§4.2): the design wants fast flicks to
  stiffen and slow presses to soften — impossible in a single flow index. The
  rate-dependence moves into the *yield stress*
  (`τ_y^eff = τ_y(S)·ξ·(1+(γ̇/γ̇_c)^q)`) while post-yield flow stays
  shear-thinning. Honest unification, real rheology.
- **Solidity-modulated Herschel–Bulkley law**: one field S ∈ [0,1) spans
  liquid → locked; locking is the S→1 limit (τ_y → ∞), not a flag. The three
  lock tools reduce to `set_solidity(mask, S)`.
- **Viscosity-modulated XPBD compliance** (§5.2): `α = 1/(k₀·g(η_app))` — the
  engineering bridge from constitutive law to a stable 60 fps solver.
- Settling as overdamped gradient flow of an explicit energy functional,
  terminated by strain-rate threshold; assimilation as parameter diffusion;
  deterministic genetic operators (inject, mitose, bind); agent grammar with
  worked examples; the seven invariants as executable specification;
  R1–R4 stated as designed experiments with binary exit criteria.
- Honesty kept where a hype paper would lie: token economy flagged as
  projected-not-measured; no implementation yet; cross-hardware float
  determinism may force fixed-point; accessibility unsolved.

Theory frozen at this document.

## 2026-07-19: 004 — R1+R2 pass: headless Rust prototype (analysis/001)

Built the dependency-free (pure `std`, single-threaded) Rust crate
implementing the full constitutive law and XPBD solver. **Both gates pass.**

- **R1 PASS**: 50 regions (1,250 particles) at ~1.2–1.4 ms/frame vs a 16 ms
  budget (~13× headroom). Scaling probe: 400 regions / 10,000 particles at
  11.8 ms — still real-time. Settles in 801 frames to max_speed exactly 0.
- **R2 PASS**: 100 independent settle runs bit-identical (FNV-1a hash
  `0xdb5295e7d7bce689`), and the same hash across separate process
  invocations. Determinism by construction: fixed dt, fixed constraint order,
  index-order reductions, seeded init, single thread.
- **9/9 tests green**: invariants I2 (law is real), I3 (locking is S→1),
  I4 (threshold-terminated settling), R2 bit-identity, confinement, plus four
  rheology unit properties.
- **Four engineering corrections discovered** (the real value — invisible
  from the equations, later normative in v0.2 as C1–C4):
  1. Non-penetration must be stiff for every material; softness lives in
     internal deformation, never in whether matter may interpenetrate
     (softness-scaled contacts jammed at 724 persistent overlaps).
  2. "Overdamped" means little carried momentum (~0.2), not heavy damping —
     retaining 90% velocity is under-damped and produced exact deterministic
     limit cycles.
  3. Thixotropy is load-bearing, not decorative: frictionless frustrated
     packings creep forever; ξ rebuilding at rest and raising the yield *is*
     the physical settle. The metaphor turned out to be the mechanism.
  4. Initial conditions are part of the contract: jittered-grid seeding
     settles cleanly; a jammed clump is pathological.
- Honest caveats recorded: cross-machine determinism untested; parameters
  tuned, not derived; 5×5 blobs, no true rigid content inclusions yet.
- Artifacts: `analysis/001/` (solver.rs, rheology.rs, invariants.rs,
  R1R2_REPORT.txt, settled.png).

## 2026-07-19: 005 — R3+R4 pass: agent grammar and expression registry (analysis/002)

The remaining two research gates, both pure software. **Both pass** — all
four gates R1–R4 now have passing, reproducible artifacts (15 automated
tests green in the packaged crate).

- **R3 PASS — agent grammar / token economy**: grammar lowered end-to-end
  into the R1 solver (parse → build World → settle → hash, reproducible), so
  "settles unambiguously" is demonstrated, not asserted. Token cost measured
  with tiktoken cl100k_base against fair minimal HTML+CSS equivalents:
  dashboard 68 / article 47 / settings 52 tokens — all under the 80-token
  criterion, **2.43× cheaper** overall. The measured saving is the floor; the
  structural claim (zero re-authoring on content/viewport change) is
  additional.
- **R4 PASS — expression registry**: CSV → chart, MP4 → player, TXT → reader
  as distinct phenotypes; a fourth type (PNG → image-viewer) added through
  the public `register_type` call with the core `sequence`/`express` path
  untouched — "no core change" is structural, since both detection and
  expression are registry-driven. Unknown types express germline `panel`.
  Deterministic: same bytes, same phenotype, every time.
- Artifacts: `analysis/002/` (grammar.rs, genetics.rs, dashboard.nnui,
  R3_REPORT.txt, R4_REPORT.txt).

## 2026-07-19: 006 — Workstream B visual bench: rejection, rebuild, arrest mechanism (analysis/003–004)

The browser-based visual bench (`nnui_cell_bench.html`) — workstream B, the
thesis made visible. Its history is the project's canonical drift example and
recovery:

- **v1 rejected**: shipped unseen, it rendered sixteen discrete dot-grids
  floating in space that never took the vessel's shape — the negation of the
  continuum thesis. Two real failures: no actual metaball field, and no fill
  mechanism. Retained in the record (`analysis/003`) as the drift example
  Invariants 1–6 exist to catch. **New standing rule: nothing visual ships
  without its rendered output captured and verified first** (Playwright +
  Chromium screenshot harness now in the toolchain).
- **Rebuild**: one continuous Herschel–Bulkley medium poured into a bowl,
  drawn as a single implicit metaball surface. Typed arrays + numeric spatial
  hash + sprite blitting brought frame cost from 18–30 ms to 8–11 ms at
  capacity (1,200 particles).
- **Settling debugged honestly, not tuned blind**. Instrumented strain
  trajectories exposed: a stale spatial hash (must rebuild every projection
  iteration, not once per tick); a violation of R1 correction #2 in the demo
  itself (88% carried momentum → strain frozen in a limit cycle at exactly
  3.313); and a lying instrument (settled reported while positions still
  advanced) → strain must be measured on realized post-arrest displacement.
- **The arrest mechanism emerged** (later formalized in v0.2 §7): yield
  deadband (sub-yield displacement reverted — below yield there is no flow;
  the material holds residual stress at rest), structure ratchet (ξ
  multiplies the yield, so slowing matter ratchets to an exact stop; rebuild
  suspended while the vessel accelerates), and jamming latch (caged rattle is
  macroscopically rest).
- **Verified programmatically**, not by eyeball: settled matter is a single
  connected component spanning the vessel in every state; a slosh visibly
  displaces the pool and re-settles in under a second; full capacity settles
  in ~5 s to strain exactly 0 with zero settled-state flicker over 10 s;
  locked state amber-verified by channel analysis.
- Artifacts: `analysis/004/` (final bench + README). The Rust crate remains
  the reference of record; the bench illustrates.

## 2026-07-20: 007 — NNUI_CELL_PoC v0.2: post-validation revision

The spec revised against evidence (`latex/v0.2/NNUI_CELL_PoC_v0.2.tex`,
14 pages; supersedes v0.1). **The continuum theory of v0.1 is unchanged** —
theory remains frozen; only its discrete realization is sharpened by
measurement.

- The four R1 corrections admitted as **normative** (§6, C1–C4): stiff
  topological constraints vs viscosity-modulated material constraints;
  overdamped predictor with carry c ≈ 0.2; thixotropy as the settle
  mechanism; spawn placement as part of the injection contract.
- **Arrest mechanism formalized** (§7): yield deadband, structure ratchet,
  jamming latch, honest strain measurement — making "settled" an exact,
  honestly measured state (‖γ̇‖∞ = 0, flicker-free).
- **Invariant 4 sharpened**: the settle predicate must read realized
  post-arrest displacement, never a damped or zeroed velocity variable.
- **Experiment plan converted to results**: R1–R4 all reported PASS with
  measured numbers; workstream B bench recorded as corroboration, including
  the honest account of its rejected first version.
- Limitations rewritten against evidence: prototype scale (no true rigid
  inclusions yet), tuned-not-derived constants, cross-hardware determinism
  still untested, token economy measured narrowly, bench constants differ
  from crate.
- Pipeline position: specification → R1–R4 prototype *(done)* → visual demo
  *(done)* → **agent-facing API (workstream A, the goal)** → integration.
- Repository restructured: `latex/v0.1/`, `latex/v0.2/`, `analysis/001–004/`,
  `logs/devlog`, `docs/research/methods.md`.

